**Update 2026-07-11 (Opus, real-mode E2E done):** A Replit checkpoint restore (`0773a8f`) had reverted `c7f2842` — re-applied it (`.replit` `outputType=webview` + `VITE_MOCK=0`; `server/index.ts` `delete process.env.VITE_MOCK`). Without `outputType=webview` the Run panel shows logs not the app ("app doesn't run"). Then ran real-mode E2E (mint JWT w/ JWT_SECRET → create client+quote for merchant 22 → open `/trades/quote/:token`) and found+fixed TWO real-mode-only bugs mock verification missed:
1. **"view quote" step skipped on first load** — server marked the quote `viewed` on the same GET the client read, so `viewedAt` was always set and the client jumped to "confirm". Fix: server returns pre-mutation `previouslyViewed` (`quote.status !== "sent"`); client decides opening step once via a `didInitQuoteStep` ref.
2. **Stray PDF popup on confirm** — `openQuotePdf()` fired on both the view and confirm branches (checkout.tsx button onClick). Fix: only open the PDF on the "view" step.
Verified E2E: first load shows "view quote"; click opens PDF + →confirm; confirm accepts w/ no popup → `$250 · 10% deposit of $2,500` payment step; revisit of accepted quote jumps to payment. `tsc` green, `npm run build` green. Changes uncommitted. Restart the Repl workflow so `.replit` webview takes effect.

